--- Rosetta Code: Include a file
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Include_a_file
--- `use` includes another source file: `use include_a_file_lib` reads
--- include_a_file_lib.co beside this file (a path such as `use lib/shapes` or
--- `use lib.shapes` reads lib/shapes.co), and what it declares is reached
--- through its name. `use include_a_file_lib as lib` would name it `lib`.

use include_a_file_lib

log[include_a_file_lib.greeting]
log[include_a_file_lib.shout['included']]

start = include_a_file_lib.origin[]
there = include_a_file_lib.moved[start, 3, 4]
log['moved from `start` to `there`']
log['a distance of `include_a_file_lib.distance[start, there]`']

corner = include_a_file_lib.Point[6, 8]
log['and `corner` is `include_a_file_lib.distance[start, corner]` from the origin']
